{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon","id":1510840,"title":"Goratrix turning himself into a Dragon!?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-05T17:25:12-07:00","id":1510840,"title":"Goratrix turning himself into a Dragon!?","content":"Since when that happened? I've read plenty of books over the course of years of storytelling (about a decade and half) and I've never came across Goratrix turning himself into a dragon or anything similar, yet one of these days I've heard from 2 different sources this story (one of them didn't have a source and the other pointed me to some pages in the 20th years anniversary edition VTM, yet I searched the book and couldn't find anything). Is it a fan theory? Is there any story in any of the books published where this sort of thing might have happened?<br /> I'm genuinely curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T19:41:07-07:00","id":1510851,"title":"","content":"The closest I've read to anything like this is an 8th level Vicissitude skill that allows kindred to breathe fire and a 9th level Vicissitude ability where they transform into a dragon or something similar to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T19:55:46-07:00","id":1510852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon#post1510840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since when that happened? I've read plenty of books over the course of years of storytelling (about a decade and half) and I've never came across Goratrix turning himself into a dragon or anything similar, yet one of these days I've heard from 2 different sources this story (one of them didn't have a source and the other pointed me to some pages in the 20th years anniversary edition VTM, yet I searched the book and couldn't find anything). Is it a fan theory? Is there any story in any of the books published where this sort of thing might have happened?<br /> I'm genuinely curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I don't think such a thing ever happened. <br /> There is a level 9 koldunic Ritual and a level 9 vicissitude one but I sincerely doubt Goratrix learned either of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T21:19:54-07:00","id":1510854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1510851#post1510851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest I've read to anything like this is an 8th level Vicissitude skill that allows kindred to breathe fire and a 9th level Vicissitude ability where they transform into a dragon or something similar to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Protean level 8 power (rather lackluster, by the way) that allows the vampire to turn into a mythological beast of his choosing and the example listed by the book is a dragon it's in the VDA20, another is Vicissitude level 9 that allows one to turn into a REALLY scary dragon that can cause &quot;Forces&quot; level of damage with his fire breath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No I don't think such a thing ever happened.<br /> There is a level 9 koldunic Ritual and a level 9 vicissitude one but I sincerely doubt Goratrix learned either of them.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Yes, this Koldunic Ritual was in revised, if I'm not mistaken in the book &quot;Blood Magic: Secrets of Thaumaturgy&quot;, but it seems to have been &quot;kind of&quot; replaced by the new Vicissitude 9 power. And yes, from what I gather Goratrix isn't that proficient with Vicissitude or Koldunic Sorcery, on the other hand, he has Thaumaturgy 9, so it would be within the realm of possibility without a doubt, but what made me curious was the story circulating and not the powers themselves, because I have read at least more than 90% of Vampires books ever published and NEVER ever heard of any such story before. I was even excited for a moment to learn that I could have one more interesting story about Goratrix to read, but tbh I guessed from the start that this hearsay wasn't true. Just posted here to know if anyone has any idea where did this story start and possibly why lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T21:55:03-07:00","id":1510858,"title":"","content":"Never heard of such a thing as either canon or fanon - where were you told of this story? Not like i've ever seen that much detail on Goratrix personality or powerset but doesn't really sound like something that &quot;jives&quot; with him.<br /> <br /> Maybe Vykos if it <b>really</b> went into a &quot;<i>i wanna be <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DTDb4G-v9zw\" target=\"_blank\">Maleficent </a>fabulous</i>!&quot; bender. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (That is <b>totally</b> going to be a thing in my version of his siege on Milwaukee from BJD <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, it could put all the Gargoyle experimentation in a whole new light and perspective - supposing that Goratrix did have an actual, personal hand in their development and wasn't just Virstania's boss/patron getting political beenies for it by association, that is.<br /> <br /> [Though the fact the Sabbat doesn't have a <b>much</b> greater number of Gargoyles in its ranks makes me suspect, DA continuity notwithstanding, he was more of the later]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-06-2023, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T22:38:06-07:00","id":1510861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe Vykos if it <b>really</b> went into a &quot;<i>i wanna be <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DTDb4G-v9zw\" target=\"_blank\">Maleficent </a>fabulous</i>!&quot; bender. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (That is <b>totally</b> going to be a thing in my version of his siege on Milwaukee from BJD <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)\u200b </div> </div> </div>Hahaha I laughed out loud with that! Marvelous! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> where were you told of this story? </div> </div> </div>Now my friend mentioned that Chat GPT said it was canon and a &quot;popular fan theory&quot; and I saw that it was true that ChatGPT did say that to him (I saw the screen), but from where did it take such information is a mystery to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, it could put all the Gargoyle experimentation in a whole new light and perspective - supposing that Goratrix did have an actual, personal hand in their development and wasn't just Virstania's boss/patron getting political beenies for it by association, that is. </div> </div> </div>I prefer to believe he did, <i>House of Tremere's</i> story of Virstania doing most (but <b>not</b> all) of the hard work, while interesting on one side (creating more interesting Tremere characters for the setting), kind of contradicts the information provided before by the setting (not to mention it kind of steals a great deal of Goratrix's spotlight concerning the Gargoyles creation) and I prefer to think that Goratrix was really the only relevant creator of the creatures and leave Virstania as the sidenote she ended up being, despite <i>House of Tremere</i> attempt, she was barely ever mentioned after that.<br /> <br /> But now, regarding the Gargoyle experimentation and the possibility of relating it to a &quot;greater project&quot;, like a way of &quot;transcending the cainite curse&quot; or something along these lines is an interesting concept for sure for more &quot;high end&quot; games and that would kind of &quot;jive&quot; with Goratrix.<br /> <br /> But I'm still <b>very</b> curious lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T00:52:45-07:00","id":1510865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1510854#post1510854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a Protean level 8 power (rather lackluster, by the way) that allows the vampire to turn into a mythological beast of his choosing and the example listed by the book is a dragon it's in the VDA20, another is Vicissitude level 9 that allows one to turn into a REALLY scary dragon that can cause &quot;Forces&quot; level of damage with his fire breath.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, this Koldunic Ritual was in revised, if I'm not mistaken in the book &quot;Blood Magic: Secrets of Thaumaturgy&quot;, but it seems to have been &quot;kind of&quot; replaced by the new Vicissitude 9 power. And yes, from what I gather Goratrix isn't that proficient with Vicissitude or Koldunic Sorcery, on the other hand, he has Thaumaturgy 9, so it would be within the realm of possibility without a doubt, but what made me curious was the story circulating and not the powers themselves, because I have read at least more than 90% of Vampires books ever published and NEVER ever heard of any such story before. I was even excited for a moment to learn that I could have one more interesting story about Goratrix to read, but tbh I guessed from the start that this hearsay wasn't true. Just posted here to know if anyone has any idea where did this story start and possibly why lol</div> </div> </div> </div>That Ritual was in libellus sanguinus btw. Yeah a Shame because Goratrix is such an interesting character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T01:02:00-07:00","id":1510867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1510861#post1510861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now my friend mentioned that Chat GPT said it was canon and a &quot;popular fan theory&quot; and I saw that it was true that ChatGPT did say that to him (I saw the screen), but from where did it take such information is a mystery to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s because ChatGPT doesn\u2019t understand its output, it\u2019s not necessarily providing information, it\u2019s providing words generated by copying other information, to look like actual information. It doesn\u2019t necessarily mean it\u2019s true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T02:39:04-07:00","id":1510869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caerolion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1510867#post1510867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s because ChatGPT doesn\u2019t understand its output, it\u2019s not necessarily providing information, it\u2019s providing words generated by copying other information, to look like actual information. It doesn\u2019t necessarily mean it\u2019s true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chat GPT told me Jack the Ripper was a member of the Whitechapel gang. Apparently we needed AI to solve the case <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T03:13:25-07:00","id":1510871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caerolion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1510867#post1510867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s because ChatGPT doesn\u2019t understand its output, it\u2019s not necessarily providing information, it\u2019s providing words generated by copying other information, to look like actual information. It doesn\u2019t necessarily mean it\u2019s true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really feel for teachers if kids start ( who am I kidding they already are) using ChatGPT to write assignments for them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T13:31:24-07:00","id":1510909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1510865#post1510865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That Ritual was in libellus sanguinus btw. Yeah a Shame because Goratrix is such an interesting character.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, my bad, I've just read it to confirm it, it's indeed in <b><i>Libellus Sanguinis: Masters of the State</i></b>. I don't know why I had this impression, wasn't it also published in another supplement? Anyway, yes Goratrix is a very interesting character and one that in my opinion could've been used more often, he makes a great &quot;genius sorcerer/inventor&quot; type of antagonist. I've used him plenty of times in the last 2 decades, but I've never came across this &quot;fan theory&quot; of him turning himself into a dragon hahaha.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That\u2019s because ChatGPT doesn\u2019t understand its output, it\u2019s not necessarily providing information, it\u2019s providing words generated by copying other information, to look like actual information. It doesn\u2019t necessarily mean it\u2019s true. </div> </div> </div>Yes and I then asked it to tell me the source and it then apologized for the mistake, but it kept committing the same mistake, that's why I wondered if it was taking information on the web, perhaps, that it was an idea used by some people in some stories, etc. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T16:59:33-07:00","id":1510928,"title":"","content":"Again, that\u2019s because it doesn\u2019t understand its output. You\u2019re not \u201cconversing\u201d with it, each time you ask it something it looks at its list of other similar questions/responses, and makes something up that looks like it\u2019d fit in with the other answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T17:30:19-07:00","id":1510934,"title":"","content":"ChatGPT will fabricate things. It is known to create false footnotes and references.<br /> <br /> I think you can safely ignore it since nobody knows the reference. On the other hand, if you are wanting a crossover with Dark Sun, you now have an excuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T18:37:05-07:00","id":1510943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is known to create false footnotes and references. </div> </div> </div>Yes, when I asked for the source it answered saying it was in VtM on pages 392-396 or something and I naturally checked in the book and there was nothing there regarding such events, so then it apologized and said it mixed up information or something lol. Quite funny I'd say, in any case the whole story ended up inspiring me with some ideas, tying the creation of the Gargoyles in a concept of transcending the curse, in a similar vein to the <b><i>via mutationis</i></b>. That might end up being useful for a future story (or maybe not lol, in any case, it's fun to write crazy ideas), I'm still concocting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if you are wanting a crossover with Dark Sun, you now have an excuse. </div> </div> </div>You got me curious there, you meant <i>Dark Sun</i> as in the D&amp;D setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T19:42:12-07:00","id":1510948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1510871#post1510871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really feel for teachers if kids start ( who am I kidding they already are) using ChatGPT to write assignments for them...</div> </div> </div> </div>I recently saw on Twitter someone reached out to a journalist asking permission to use a quote of his. The thing is, the quote wasn't his. ChatGPT created a quote and attributed it to the journalist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T20:22:43-07:00","id":1510952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1510943#post1510943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You got me curious there, you meant <i>Dark Sun</i> as in the D&amp;D setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, as that is the setting where the wizard-kings turn themselves into dragons.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T20:28:53-07:00","id":1510954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1510871#post1510871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really feel for teachers if kids start ( who am I kidding they already are) using ChatGPT to write assignments for them...</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a friend who's a freshman teacher. She's held several lessons for her class on how students should use and approach ChatGPT. She says students are going to be using it no matter what, and it will give a huge advantage to those who have access to it and those who don't, so she wants to show them how to use it as a tool for learning, and to understand how to use it to help them learn. She's also making sure they understand that ChatGPT will give you an answer to your question, but if that doesn't mean the answer will be true, and often times it will just give you false information but make it look accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T01:00:06-07:00","id":1510962,"title":"","content":"There are many stories about heroes, leaders, explorers, and researchers who come the Tremere Antitribu that mention beautiful and amazing abilities, items, situations, and achievements. However from what I have found and read, Goratrix taking upon an aspect of a dragon or gaining draconic characteristics is not among the currently existing descriptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T14:22:50-07:00","id":1511019,"title":"","content":"As an aside regarding Gargoyle creation, I dislike having Goratrix be the lone genius in the Tremere who built Ceoris, came up with the foundational ritual to turn wizards into vampires, AND invented Gargoyles. (What next, did he come up with the curse on the Assamites all by his lonesome?) Virstania being the real innovator and Goratrix getting the lion's share of the credit by managing the process strategically to the benefit of the clan suits me better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T19:49:12-07:00","id":1511040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, as that is the setting where the wizard-kings turn themselves into dragons.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>Hahaha, I think it's a bit hard to make something like that work in a Vampire game, as I stated, seeing the process of &quot;turning into a dragon&quot; on a more metaphysical level of transcending the curse is more interesting to explore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have a friend who's a freshman teacher. She's held several lessons for her class on how students should use and approach ChatGPT. She says students are going to be using it no matter what, and it will give a huge advantage to those who have access to it and those who don't, so she wants to show them how to use it as a tool for learning, and to understand how to use it to help them learn. She's also making sure they understand that ChatGPT will give you an answer to your question, but if that doesn't mean the answer will be true, and often times it will just give you false information but make it look accurate. </div> </div> </div>I also believe that is a necessary discussion, we need to be honest regarding that with our students. Naturally, any kid who uses it would have a huge advantage over the ones who don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As an aside regarding Gargoyle creation, I dislike having Goratrix be the lone genius in the Tremere who built Ceoris, came up with the foundational ritual to turn wizards into vampires, AND invented Gargoyles. (What next, did he come up with the curse on the Assamites all by his lonesome?) Virstania being the real innovator and Goratrix getting the lion's share of the credit by managing the process strategically to the benefit of the clan suits me better. </div> </div> </div>I believe you have a good point there, by the way let's not forget he also invented artificial blood (however useless it ended up being, it's still cool lol), was one of the creators of the blood brothers, was directly responsible for the end of the Templar, for the destruction of a bizarre monster/creature/entity in Mexico, among other things hahaha <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. As I said, you have a good point there, and I can easily see her being more important to the process of creation of the Gargoyles and master Goratrix by employing them on a strategical level in the war against the Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T19:33:48-07:00","id":1511098,"title":"","content":"Tremere's body turned into a white worm, and Tremere stole Goratrix's body (Goratrix is in a mirror). Maybe ChatGPT read &quot;white worm&quot; as &quot;white wyrm&quot; and got muddled by all the body hopping, assuming Goratrix was a dragon as a result. That's all I've got.<br /> <br /> Still, Goratrix as a dragon would be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T22:14:40-07:00","id":1511106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1511098#post1511098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tremere's body turned into a white worm, and Tremere stole Goratrix's body (Goratrix is in a mirror). Maybe ChatGPT read &quot;white worm&quot; as &quot;white wyrm&quot; and got muddled by all the body hopping, assuming Goratrix was a dragon as a result. That's all I've got.<br /> <br /> Still, Goratrix as a dragon would be cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually makes a lot of sense, perhaps it was this confusion.<br /> <br /> And yes, I also think Goratrix as a dragon would be very cool hahaha.<br /> <br /> PS: By the way, if I'm not mistaken, DAV20 France had a Cainite that could turn into a dragon and it wasn't even because of a power, it was something related to her having a spirit of a dragon inside her or something along these lines, I need to reread with attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T11:00:55-07:00","id":1511139,"title":"","content":"Maybe a bit unrelated but I kind of like the idea in a certain context.<br /> <br /> I am a bit of a fan of the Dark Souls games and other fromsoftware titles. In Dark Souls and even in the more recent title Elden Ring one can find mortals with the goal of turning themselves into dragons, because they admire them as perfect immortal beings (I am aware thats a rather general, surface level statement but I wanted to keep it short). The thing is though these experiments and transformations mostly result in a horribly corrupted and deformed existence. In a way this would fit nicely into the WOD.<br /> <br /> Relating that to Goratrix as the one who created the Ritual of Usurpation to grant immortality to him and the Council of Seven the &quot;turning himself into a dragon&quot; could be seen as a metaphor to reach &quot;perfect immortality&quot;, through the &quot;Dragonblood&quot; (Tzimisce Elder Blood) that he stole.<br /> <br /> Oh well just a little rambling... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T11:07:06-07:00","id":1511141,"title":"","content":"ChatGPT is absolute garbage for doing any serious course work or assignments. I hate that these AI chatbot things have become popular (don't accuse me of being a ludd' tho, lol). Especially more now, since apparently ChatGPT just gives out blatantly false information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T11:26:21-07:00","id":1511144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1511019#post1511019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside regarding Gargoyle creation, I dislike having Goratrix be the lone genius in the Tremere who built Ceoris, came up with the foundational ritual to turn wizards into vampires, AND invented Gargoyles. (What next, did he come up with the curse on the Assamites all by his lonesome?) Virstania being the real innovator and Goratrix getting the lion's share of the credit by managing the process strategically to the benefit of the clan suits me better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually really hated finding out about the &quot;mother of Gargoyles&quot;. What I once thought of as a cool and noble slave revolt turns out to either be motherhood impulses (as I read it from LotB) or some elder machination. It really undermined the Gargoyle position for me. <br /> <br /> <br /> On the other topic, given the power disparity between vampires, and the number of years they operate with, it makes sense that some vampires get disproportionate achievements, especially in a young clan like Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T11:26:33-07:00","id":1511145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacedigger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1511139#post1511139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a bit unrelated but I kind of like the idea in a certain context.<br /> <br /> I am a bit of a fan of the Dark Souls games and other fromsoftware titles. In Dark Souls and even in the more recent title Elden Ring one can find mortals with the goal of turning themselves into dragons, because they admire them as perfect immortal beings (I am aware thats a rather general, surface level statement but I wanted to keep it short). The thing is though these experiments and transformations mostly result in a horribly corrupted and deformed existence. In a way this would fit nicely into the WOD.<br /> <br /> Relating that to Goratrix as the one who created the Ritual of Usurpation to grant immortality to him and the Council of Seven the &quot;turning himself into a dragon&quot; could be seen as a metaphor to reach &quot;perfect immortality&quot;, through the &quot;Dragonblood&quot; (Tzimisce Elder Blood) that he stole.<br /> <br /> Oh well just a little rambling... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really nice taking, by the way I'm also a fan of the Dark Souls series and I remember I once told a friend that many themes explored in Dark Souls ressonate with the WoD in a way or could be easily adapted. I love the atmosphere of the game and I use the games' soundtrack in my Dark Ages games as I find them very fitting. <br /> <br /> Yes, Goratrix using the blood of the &quot;Dragons&quot; to attain immortality is a perfect metaphor to reach &quot;perfect immortality&quot;, I'm currently brainstorming some ideas relating his whole enterprise of creating the <i>Ritual of Usurpation </i>and the Gargoyles to a greater theme.<br /> <br /> As I suspected, in DAV20 France there is a cainite possessed by a shard of the spirit of a Black Dragon Sorcerer, she's called Zyrlane a priestess of the Black Dragon Zinitra (that is based on Slav Mythology, Zinitra is the Black Dragon god of magic in slav paganism) and it seems the shard of the Dragon Spirit inside her wants to reunite with the other parts, in any case, every night he takes control of her and she assumes the form of a black dragon, it even has stats for the form.As I mentioned, it seems she's in search of the other shards of the Black Dragon Spirit. DAV20 France is such a wonderful and gorgeous book that it's a shame it wasn't translated into English, it's not only beautiful, but has many interesting story ideas and characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T07:58:37-07:00","id":1511221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1511145#post1511145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a really nice taking, by the way I'm also a fan of the Dark Souls series and I remember I once told a friend that many themes explored in Dark Souls ressonate with the WoD in a way or could be easily adapted. I love the atmosphere of the game and I use the games' soundtrack in my Dark Ages games as I find them very fitting.<br /> <br /> Yes, Goratrix using the blood of the &quot;Dragons&quot; to attain immortality is a perfect metaphor to reach &quot;perfect immortality&quot;, I'm currently brainstorming some ideas relating his whole enterprise of creating the <i>Ritual of Usurpation </i>and the Gargoyles to a greater theme.<br /> <br /> As I suspected, in DAV20 France there is a cainite possessed by a shard of the spirit of a Black Dragon Sorcerer, she's called Zyrlane a priestess of the Black Dragon Zinitra (that is based on Slav Mythology, Zinitra is the Black Dragon god of magic in slav paganism) and it seems the shard of the Dragon Spirit inside her wants to reunite with the other parts, in any case, every night he takes control of her and she assumes the form of a black dragon, it even has stats for the form.As I mentioned, it seems she's in search of the other shards of the Black Dragon Spirit. DAV20 France is such a wonderful and gorgeous book that it's a shame it wasn't translated into English, it's not only beautiful, but has many interesting story ideas and characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The concept of eventual corruption and rot of everything as it is portrayed in the souls universe is something I allude to in my WOD games, although not in a world ending scale.<br /> <br /> Your idea sounds very interesting but it seems to fit a rather specific chronicle. It is something I struggle with from time to time. Not every story hook fits every chronicle imho.<br /> <br /> DAV20 France sounds really kickass! Kinda regret not having appreciated my six years of learning french in school and unlearning it in a matter of a year ^^'. But the book itself I found to be evry evocativ from scimming character articles on white wolf wiki. The Art is absolutely gorgeous.<br /> <br /> I am more of Antiquity guy when it comes to Vampire. Soon I'll be starting a chronicle in Ancient Mesopotamia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:09:36-07:00","id":1511257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacedigger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1511221#post1511221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The concept of eventual corruption and rot of everything as it is portrayed in the souls universe is something I allude to in my WOD games, although not in a world ending scale.<br /> <br /> Your idea sounds very interesting but it seems to fit a rather specific chronicle. It is something I struggle with from time to time. Not every story hook fits every chronicle imho.<br /> <br /> DAV20 France sounds really kickass! Kinda regret not having appreciated my six years of learning french in school and unlearning it in a matter of a year ^^'. But the book itself I found to be evry evocativ from scimming character articles on white wolf wiki. The Art is absolutely gorgeous.<br /> <br /> I am more of Antiquity guy when it comes to Vampire. Soon I'll be starting a chronicle in Ancient Mesopotamia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, my ideas are very specific, I'd say, but I've never been a fan of &quot;Elysium games&quot;, so we're kind of used to it around here. The themes I explore, wouldn't work nearly as good in a modern setting, in fact I've never been a fan of modern settings either. DAV20 France is definitely one of the best investments in terms of scenario books I've seen in the WoD over all these years.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T04:11:41-07:00","id":1511535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacedigger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1511221#post1511221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am more of Antiquity guy when it comes to Vampire. Soon I'll be starting a chronicle in Ancient Mesopotamia.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may ask - in this Chronicle what is the state of invention, science and knowledge - related advancements and progression ? Or otherwise stated - what is the technological, political social, religious and cultural level and background ? <br /> Will there be any particular elements and differences introduced from the wider World of Darkness RPG, or from other fantasy and supernatural settings ?<br /> <br /> I have played games like Skyrim, Civilization 4, Age of Mythology, Medieval: Total War 2 and Heroes of Might and Magic 5 extensively, so the topic of technological, social, and cultural progression, research, and advancments does interest me to a considerable and significant extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T09:38:05-07:00","id":1511875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510840-goratrix-turning-himself-into-a-dragon?p=1511535#post1511535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may ask - in this Chronicle what is the state of invention, science and knowledge - related advancements and progression ? Or otherwise stated - what is the technological, political social, religious and cultural level and background ?<br /> Will there be any particular elements and differences introduced from the wider World of Darkness RPG, or from other fantasy and supernatural settings ?<br /> <br /> I have played games like Skyrim, Civilization 4, Age of Mythology, Medieval: Total War 2 and Heroes of Might and Magic 5 extensively, so the topic of technological, social, and cultural progression, research, and advancments does interest me to a considerable and significant extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello there and sorry for the late reply I do not have Email notifications enabled ^^'<br /> <br /> Thats a rather good question. I'll try my best.<br /> <br /> Most of the background for the chronicle is based on a, imho, excellent Storytellers Vault supplement called &quot;Vampire: Age of the Living Gods&quot;. It of course deviates from established canon but to me and my group that is no problem at all.<br /> <br /> The supplement is set 2350 BCE in the &quot;Fertile Crescent&quot; region, which is a rather large region consisting of many contemporary countries like Irak, Syria e.g.<br /> <br /> The supplement sets in a century after the Fall of the Second City in VTM.<br /> <br /> The political situation is that of city-states like Uruk, Ur and Akkad eg. ruled by kings during the day and &quot;Living Gods&quot; and their Heralds during the Night. You can probably see where this going ^^'<br /> <br /> These &quot;Living Gods&quot; are predominantly the surviving Antedeluvians like Arikel (Ishtar during that time), Cappadocius and Saulot (Ashur during that time, this special case is left deliberatly vague in the book), Troile (as Anat) and Ennoia (as Ereshkigal). More living gods are coming from the ranks of the future Methusalehs so from the 4th and 5th Generation. With some exceptions every City in the region has a Living God that feeds on blood sacrifices made by the kine. Everything in kindred society revolves around these blood sacrifices and the kindred have constructed a literal pyramid scheme around their godhood. There are also five political factions among kindred with different or overlapping goals.<br /> <br /> Concering technological aspects and science I cannot answer that much in detail tbh. Architecure and Astrology play a pronounced role and of course agricultural development and bronce/copper metallurgy.<br /> <br /> A very interesting thing the author did is that he did not shy away from certain lvls of crossover between the other WOD splats. I guess here is where it deviates the most from the established canon, since it involves Fera who should be extinct already (not an exoert on WTA lore) like the Apis. The author also incorporates some stuff from Demon the Fallen which is rather interesting.<br /> <br /> I hope that answer was satisfactory^^'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}